\section{Design}{

One design of the manuscript's corrected factorial benchmark: complete
transcriptional shutoff (\code{"SHUTOFF"}) at the common intervention time
\code{t_star = 332} min; sampling at \code{t_star - 10}, \code{t_star}, \code{t_star + 10},
\code{+ 20} and \code{+ 30} min (5 time points); 5 destructive replicates per time
point; replicate-level rate variability \code{param_cv = 0.05}; RNA-seq assay
noise at level \code{"very_low"}; integration grid \code{origin = 0},
\code{grid_step = 1}, \code{horizon = 1000}, \code{y0 = 0}. The design was selected from
the benchmark table before any data were generated. Among the
benchmark's SHUTOFF designs with at most 10 time points and 5 replicates
whose Type-I error interval contains 0.05, it had the highest power at
\code{alpha = 0.05}: about 0.24, with Type-I error 0.042. Most simulated
alternative events are therefore not expected to reach significance. The
example shows realistic uncertainty and does not guarantee detection.
